        <briefdescription>
<para>Counts the number of entities in a CUDA hierarchy level. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>Returns how many instances of Unit are in Level. Unit and Level need to be core CUDA hierarchy levels, for example <ref refid="structcuda_1_1experimental_1_1grid__level" kindref="compound">grid_level</ref> or <ref refid="structcuda_1_1experimental_1_1block__level" kindref="compound">block_level</ref>. This function is also available as a level type member function, in that case it only takes a unit argument.</para>
<para><simplesect kind="par"><title>Snippet</title><para><programlisting><codeline><highlight class="normal">#include<sp/>&lt;cudax/hierarchy_dimensions.cuh&gt;</highlight></codeline>
<codeline></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">using<sp/>namespace<sp/>cuda::experimental;</highlight></codeline>
<codeline></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">__global__<sp/>void<sp/>kernel()</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">{</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>//<sp/>Can<sp/>be<sp/>called<sp/>with<sp/>the<sp/>instances<sp/>of<sp/>level<sp/>types</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>int<sp/>num_threads_in_block<sp/>=<sp/>hierarchy::count(thread,<sp/>block);</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>int<sp/>num_blocks_in_grid<sp/>=<sp/>grid.count(block);</highlight></codeline>
<codeline></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>//<sp/>Or<sp/>using<sp/>the<sp/>level<sp/>types<sp/>as<sp/>template<sp/>arguments</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>int<sp/>num_threads_in_grid<sp/>=<sp/>hierarchy::count&lt;thread_level,<sp/>grid_level&gt;();</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">}</highlight></codeline>
</programlisting> </para>
</simplesect>
